From cabe54eb82941893b9b5188b1628c3a27884351f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Taylor <miketaylr@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:40:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/32] [css] Reset element sheet when <meta name="referrer">
 changes policy

Follow-up to https://crrev.com/c/8602043, which made inline CSS snapshot
the owner document's referrer policy at parse time.

`Document::ElementSheet()` is created lazily and cached, and its parser
context is used for every inline `style` attribute and presentation
attribute. If it was created before `<meta name="referrer">` was
processed (for example by `<meta name="color-scheme">`, which parses
its content with the element sheet's context), later inline styles kept
the stale pre-meta policy and could send a referrer under
`no-referrer`.

When `<meta name="referrer">` changes the document's policy, drop
`elem_sheet_` (as `Document::UpdateBaseURL()` already does for base URL
changes) and clear `StyleEngine`'s cached `fill`/`clip-path`
`CSSURIValue`s, which were parsed with the old element sheet context.

A policy from the `Referrer-Policy` header is applied before the
document is created, so it does not need this invalidation.

Bug: 392139161
Change-Id: Ib688e41c7c78cbc201993af85b513652198233d6
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8603655
